{
  "schema": "visagames.tapLetter.wordBank.v1",
  "version": 1,
  "updated": "2026-10-22",
  "author": "Opus 5.5 (design only; see ../design.md §7)",
  "notes": [
    "Lowercase only in v1. Child-facing letters and word labels are drawn with the house centerline glyphs (latin:<x>), never with a font.",
    "gloss_zh is HK Traditional Chinese for the parent pages only. The child never sees it.",
    "status: full = curated and ready for art; anchor_only = only the anchor is approved, candidates are a draft for Carter to review.",
    "tier: core = clean onset (consonant + vowel, or a short vowel) and very familiar to a 4-year-old; extra = consonant blend, longer or less familiar. Extra words join a letter's deck only when the letter reaches box 2 (熟緊).",
    "highlight = [start, length] of the letters drawn in teal on the flipped card (the target letter). For x the target sits at the end (box) or middle (taxi).",
    "article = the article used before the letter name in speech: 'Here's an a!' / 'Here's a d!'.",
    "name.ipa is sent to the TTS with AVSpeechSynthesisIPANotationAttribute, so a lone 'a' is never read as the article 'uh'. z is 'zed' (British).",
    "sound.* is reserved for human recordings of pure sounds (/d/ not 'duh'); the 'Letter sounds' setting stays off until the clips exist."
  ],

  "rules": {
    "zh": [
      "開頭字母 = 開頭音，而且係嗰個字母最常見嘅音（c 用 cat 唔用 circle、chair；g 用 goat 唔用 giraffe；s 唔用 ship；t 唔用 thumb；k 唔用 knife；母音用短音：apple、egg、igloo、octopus、umbrella）。",
      "x 例外：用「x 喺尾」嘅字（box、fox），翻牌字標住 x 嗰個位。",
      "4 歲識、畫得出、一眼認得嘅實物名詞。",
      "英式英文、香港用法（lorry、tap 係水喉）。",
      "冇品牌（唔用 jeep、Lego）。",
      "唔嚇人、唔危險（唔用 shark、snake、spider、knife、axe）；動物畫友善樣。",
      "一張圖一個叫法（唔用 bat：蝙蝠定球棒）。",
      "子音群（tr、dr、pl、st、sn…）放 extra。",
      "有車就放（佢鍾意），但唔搶晒每個字母。",
      "車身、圖入面冇字、冇數字、冇 logo。",
      "gloss_zh 用香港繁體，冇簡體字。"
    ],
    "en": [
      "Initial letter = initial sound, and it is the letter's most common sound (cat not circle/chair; goat not giraffe; no sh, ch, th, kn starts; short vowels for a e i o u).",
      "x is the exception: x words have x at the end or middle (box, fox, taxi), highlighted where it is.",
      "Concrete, picturable nouns a 4-year-old knows.",
      "British English, Hong Kong usage.",
      "No brand names.",
      "Nothing scary or dangerous; animals drawn friendly.",
      "One picture, one name (avoid bat).",
      "Consonant blends go to extra.",
      "Vehicles are welcome but must not take over every letter.",
      "No text, numbers or logos inside pictures.",
      "gloss_zh is HK Traditional Chinese only."
    ]
  },

  "paths": {
